{
 "id": "20260926-193000-interaction-supervisor-relay-decompose",
 "axis": "interaction",
 "hypothesis": "The supervisor-routed response relay (worker to_vec -> supervisor from_slice Value tree -> from_value DaemonResponse -> response_line deep clone -> client-line to_string) is the dominant supervisor-side cost at Kevin-scale routed attaches: attach-path's baseline measured +14..+54ms over the direct transport at 1.45-9.48MB wire. Decompose it at the current tip and test whether the wire bytes the client receives are spliceable from the worker's own payload bytes (i.e. whether the supervisor's parse+clone+re-serialize is necessary for routing, or routing needs only the frame header's requestId plus attach bookkeeping scalars).",
 "approach": "BASELINE + DECOMPOSITION ONLY (no product edit). Pure tip 7064d039a release pa-daemon (rustc 1.98.1) on one 16c/32GB ubuntu:22.04 VM, same-VM sequential fresh-daemon probes over the REAL wire (supervisor socket routed + direct worker transport via ticket+peer_auth), 3 creates x per-fixture over attach-path's published synthetic fixtures (synth-150k, synth-450k, canonical-10mib); per fixture: routed get_session_header (floor) / get_state (1.1KB data) / get_messages (full-history data) / attach slim+legacy (fresh connection per attach), direct state/msgs/reattach/fresh-attach, per-trial fixture prehash asserted, pre/mid/post CPU calibration, raw wire dumps per kind. A second DIAGNOSTIC build (same tip + env-gated SRPHASE eprintlns in supervisor reader pump, protocol::response_line, supervisor write_line, routing.rs route wait, worker write_response_frame; PA_RELAY_TIMING only) decomposed the relay per phase; the diagnostic binary is never used for deltas. Splice oracle: routed raw line bytes vs direct raw payload bytes, per fixture, get_messages and attach.",
 "parity_notes": "no product change; this record is baseline evidence + a byte-level wire analysis. The splice proof shows the exact byte relationship the routed client line has to the worker payload: get_messages routed line == '{\"id\":\"<cid>\",' + direct worker payload[1:] byte-identical at all 3 fixtures; attach differs only in data.client (id: supervisor-assigned routed client id vs the direct request's clientId; capabilities echo) at the response tail.",
